hived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-01-28T18:08:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-04T00:03:00Z","closed_at":"2026-02-03T23:58:10Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115521","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115521","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115521.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115521.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"- Follow-up to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111047 (can be merged independently).\r\n\r\nThese are equivalent to `forward_plus` and `gl_compatibility` respectively. This does not change the name reported elsewhere (if you start with `--rendering-method compatibility`, `OS.get_current_rendering_method()` still returns `gl_compatibility`).\r\n\r\nThis makes it a bit quicker to switch renderers on the command line, which is quite common when testing rendering PRs to make sure they work correctly on all renderers.\r\n\r\nNote that like in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111047, we could also add `get_short_name()` to each rendering method implementation, but since these can't be distributed as GDExtensions, there's less point in doing that.","closed_by":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/user